    "narrative": "For today's matchup, our core offensive engine is driven by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.53) and **Brice Turang** (70.49), who represent our strongest plays. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from a dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed arm, while **Brice Turang** earns top billing due to a high-leverage matchup against Houser; the 18% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s skill profile, combined with an elite placement in the three-hole, makes him our anchor. While **Corbin Carroll** (67.04) faces a tougher test against the southpaw Wrobleski, his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in the scarce SB category. The \"slow delivery\" metric of the opposing battery adds a 4% premium to his projection, ensuring he remains a start despite the left-on-left disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the middle infield depth. While **Travis Bazzana** (48.79) draws a start, he is dangerously close to the floor, penalized heavily by the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed pitcher. We are keeping a close watch on **Austin Riley** (42.20), who remains in the lineup despite a sub-optimal 19% SP skill penalty against Fluharty. Given the current bench composition, our reserve options\u2014including **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Kyle Karros**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014did not present a higher ceiling today. **Dalton Rushing** (54.64) and **Gabriel Moreno** (54.08) are effectively holding the line; while neither is posting an elite efficiency score, their lineup stability and park factors keep them ahead of the fringe bench talent.\n\nWe are operating with heightened caution regarding the 3.22 xERA of the pitcher opposing **Austin Riley**, as his recent volatility makes that specific matchup a significant risk for a zero-for-four afternoon. Furthermore, while we monitor for late-breaking lineup changes, the status of **Josh Naylor** and **James Wood** remains N/A due to an off-day, and we continue to navigate the absence of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** due to their placement on the IL. With SB being our primary scarcity constraint, we are prioritizing **Jose Caballero** (58.29) and his 100% SB-favorable delivery matchup over safer, high-average bats to ensure we maximize our category efficiency despite the marginal score.",
